@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@
+Fix :class:`~filelock.ReadWriteLock` acting on ``-journal``, ``-wal`` or ``-shm`` files another process puts beside its
+database: a write could land in another file, a reader could get in beside a writer, and an acquire could fail. In a
+directory that other accounts can write, SQLite now opens the database through a private hard link instead of by its
+shared name, so those files are never consulted. Where hard links are unavailable there, the acquire raises
+:class:`OSError`; keep the database in a directory other accounts cannot write instead. A database whose schema takes
+more than a few kilobytes to load raises :class:`ValueError` instead of running past the acquire timeout.
